From 8f43a3b6441a9395cd6d5078be619809f1cf817e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:51:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Let the Gmail/Outlook add-ins hand off into a logged-in
 website session

Website manual uploads still require real Google OAuth login. But the
add-ins already know who the user is -- Gmail Apps Script's
Session.getActiveUser().getEmail() and Outlook's
Office.context.mailbox.userProfile.emailAddress are both identities
the mail platform itself already verified, not something a browser
user typed in. There was no bridge from that identity into the
website's session, so "VIEW FULL INVESTIGATION" would just hit the
new login wall.

- identity_required (api.py): /analyze now accepts either the browser
  session (website) or an X-API-Key + body user_id pair (add-ins) as
  proof of identity -- the API key is a secret only our own add-ins
  hold, so a client-claimed user_id is trusted only in that channel,
  never from an arbitrary browser request.
- When an add-in call succeeds, /analyze mints a short-lived (10 min)
  signed token (itsdangerous) binding that email + the new
  investigation id, returned as report_url.
- New /auth/addon-session verifies that token, sets the same session
  cookie Google OAuth would, registers the user in Neon if new, and
  redirects into the website already logged in -- so History shows
  that account's real past investigations immediately, no separate
  login step.
- GmailEmailAnalyzer.gs's "VIEW FULL INVESTIGATION" button and the
  new taskpane.js/.html "Open Full Report & History" link both use
  report_url when present.
- taskpane.js now actually sends user_id (previously missing
  entirely), read the same way from Office.context.mailbox.userProfile.
